/**
 * Real panel speech, for the echo spike only.
 *
 * PCM16, 16 kHz, mono — the wire format from `docs/voice-stream-protocol.md`,
 * so it can be played out and compared against what comes back in without a
 * conversion step in between.
 *
 * Real speech rather than the synthetic tone the acoustic spike used, because
 * this run is judged by a voice-activity detector. Both the echo canceller and
 * the VAD are tuned for speech; a harmonic stack is a fair test of acoustic
 * coupling and a poor test of whether a VAD hears words.
 *
 * Generated with macOS `say --data-format=LEI16@16000`, the same source the
 * latency spike used, so the two runs are comparable. It is checked in because
 * a phone cannot run `say`, and it leaves with the spike.
 */
export const PANEL_SPEECH_BASE64 =
  '';
